    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**New User**\\n\\nGoal: Test your model for someone new.\\n\\n1. In **Predict** and **Using**, choose the label and only the Tree 2 features from **Tree 1 vs. Tree 2** in your guide.\\n2. Click **Train model**.\\n\\nYou are done when your tree shows. Go to the **Testing** tab.\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**New User**\\n\\nGoal: Test your model for someone new.\\n\\n> Jordan studies best with soft songs that have singing. Jordan's favorite has slow piano and a singer.\\n> - Energy: it is calm, so Low.\\n> - Tempo (BPM): about 85 beats per minute. Under 90 counts as Slow.\\n> - Length (min): 5 minutes. Over 4 minutes counts as Long.\\n> - Has Lyrics: it has singing all the way through, so Yes.\\n>\\n> True answers: Study Song? Yes. Danceable? No, it is hard to dance to. Acoustic? Yes, it is piano and voice.\\n\\n1. In **Make a Prediction**, choose a category for each feature that fits this user. Write the categories you chose in **New User** in your guide.\\n2. Click **Predict**. Wait until the path stops moving. Write the prediction.\\n3. Find the label you chose in **Predict** in the **True answers** line above.\\n4. Write ✓ in your guide if the prediction matches the true answer, or ✗ if it doesn't.\\n\\nYou are done when New User in your guide is full.\"\r\n}",
